From c22b1f1a40a0935bf589d8f9ff7848d0ea7c188e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 05:09:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] Let the Lightkeeper change the circle's insignia by
 clicking it

Issue #66.7, decision 7. On the Circle page the insignia stamp of a sealed
circle is now a button, as a player's portrait is: "Change" under it opens the
eight insignia of the formation papers, the one chosen is sent at once, and
Undo puts the last one back for the portrait's eight seconds. Before the seal
the players vote for it, so the stamp is only shown, as before.

update_circle takes an insignia field: one of the eight keys, else 422 and
nothing of the message is saved; a change writes "The Lightkeeper changed the
circle's insignia to Moon." in the Activity Log. WEBSOCKET.md and FAQ.md say
so.

Checked: tests/test_ws_circle.py (new test_update_circle_insignia),
tests/test_surface.py and tests/test_ws_connect.py pass. In Chromium at
1366x768, 820x1180 and 390x844 the stamp opens the chooser, a choice reaches
the database and the log, and Undo shows under the stamp.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01ETKqHLvkfH9k99JTnJzzKA
